t all completed). pw.out: 8 electrons -> 4 occupied bands; nbnd=12 ample, no fix needed.\n- STEP 7 (plot_bands.py): parsed the real, non-empty 000.bands.dat.gnu (12 bands, 121 k-points), aligned to VBM using occupied-band count from pw.out, mapped label indices to cumulative-distance x-values (INVARIANT 4, asserted tick range matches band k-column range), split lines at repeated-x jump and labelled U|K on both sides, y restricted to +/-10 eV, saved calculations/000/bands_000.pdf.\n\nASE FUNCTIONS USED: structure I/O -- ase.io.read/write, ase.Atoms, Atoms.rattle, Atoms.set_cell/get_scaled_positions/get_atomic_numbers/cell.reciprocal; QE I/O -- ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in (SCF MP grid + explicit k-point ndarray for bands). spglib+seekpath used for symmetry/primitive reduction/k-path.\n\nBAND GAP OBTAINED: VBM=13.4503 eV, CBM=18.8931 eV, gap = 5.44 eV for the unperturbed structure_000.\n\nINVARIANTS confirmed for calculations/000: nat=2/ntyp=1 derived from the Atoms object (validate_qe_input passed); ecut Ha->Ry conversion (82.0/328.0 Ry, asserted); k-path from seekpath on the exact cell with 2*pi reprojection; occupied bands read from pw.out (8 electrons/2=4); x-axis units reconciled and asserted.\n\nSCIENTIFIC ASSUMPTIONS / JUSTIFICATION: occupations='fixed' since diamond is an insulator (no smearing needed); MP 8x8x8 dense grid well-converged for a 2-atom primitive insulator; rattle stdev 0.05 A justified by diamond's high Debye temperature; PBEsol functional per the requested pseudopotential.\n\nNEEDS EXPERT REVIEW: the 5.44 eV gap is a near-direct/indirect value taken over the sampled path and is somewhat higher than the ~4.1 eV indirect PBE(sol) value typically quoted -- this is because VBM/CBM are extracted over the finite k-path (not a dense mesh), so the reported gap may be closer to the direct gap; a physicist may want to compute the true indirect gap from a fuller k-sampling. Only calculations/000 was run per task instructions; the remaining 50 perturbed structures have inputs prepared but were not executed."}}
